WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:41.040
<b>Roger's Adventure</b>

3
00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:57.180
[sighs]
Thanks to
the help of Gan Fall,

4
00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.320
the god atop the clouds,
we descended safely.

5
00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.520
No, the South Pole!

6
00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:00.640
– The North is colder!
– The South is!

7
00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.360
The North Pole!

8
00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:02.990
You want a pole to the face?

9
00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.860
[Shanks]
Maybe if I knock your
brain around, it'll work right!

10
00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.910
That's enough, you two!

11
00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:11.080
Do you ever stop squabbling?
Knock it off!

12
00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:13.400
Now that's easy!

13
00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.110
Our new goal will be the last
island on the Grand Line.

14
00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.980
However, we will
require copies of

15
00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.820
all four Road Poneglyphs
to find its location.

16
00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:23.280
You mean like
the one we already found?

17
00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.320
There is one
in the Land of Wano.

18
00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:28.120
Yeah, our Mokomo Dukedom
has one, as well!

19
00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:31.370
All this time, you guys
had stones back at home?

20
00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.370
It's different than
the last one, though.

21
00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:34.670
[all]
– It's colored red.
– It's colored red.

22
00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:36.540
But that's the kind
I need the most!

23
00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.040
You shoulda told me sooner!

24
00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:40.260
Let's get 'em!
Then two more to go!

25
00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.720
Well. Took a little effort,

26
00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:43.680
but I nabbed a rubbing
of Linlin's stone,

27
00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:46.140
so with your help,
I'll have three!

28
00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.850
And I have a pretty good hunch
where the fourth one is.

29
00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:50.680
[Rayleigh]
Nice work, Roger!

30
00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:52.890
We're even closer
than I realized!

31
00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:56.360
Our goal is right within
our grasp! [laughs]

32
00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.820
[Gaban]
Sorry to bring the mood down,

33
00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.730
but I think that fall
really messed up our ship!

34
00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:01.900
How is it?

35
00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.860
It's hard to tell
with my untrained eye,

36
00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:05.740
but we're gonna need
some repairs, and quick.

37
00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.120
All right. Then I know
just where to go.

38
00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:08.710
And where's that?

39
00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:09.330
It's Water Seven.
The City of Water, huh?

40
00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.620
[Gold Roger]
Water 7, "The City of Water"!

41
00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.960
[Oden]
An aquatic town?

42
00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:14.580
[Toki]
Sounds romantic!

43
00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.880
[Gold Roger]
Full speed ahead! Let's go!

44
00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.300
[Roger pirates]
Yeah!

45
00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.840
[Oden]
Thus, we ventured
to a city of shipwrights

46
00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:25.880
in order to repair the damages
to Roger's beloved vessel.

47
00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:36.280
<b>Scrap Island
Water Seven</b>

48
00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.790
<b>Tom
(The Shipwright
Who Built Roger's Ship)</b>

49
00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:43.450
[Tom laughs]
Roger,
what brings you here today?

50
00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.610
Greetings, Tom!

51
00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.570
– Hey, it's good to see you!
– There he is!

52
00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:49.040
Tom! Hey!

53
00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:53.120
[Tom laughs]
Well, this is
quite the reunion, isn't it?

54
00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.060
Yeah. We've missed you, friend!

55
00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.560
[TOM laughs] [Tom laughs]

56
00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:56.560
[GOLD ROGER]
Finish that project yet?

57
00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.270
[Gold Roger]
Finish that project yet?

58
00:03:58.270 --> 00:03:58.630
You talkin' about the Sea Train?

59
00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.150
You talking about the Sea Train?

60
00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:00.550
You're crazy. That thing's
still in the design phase!

61
00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:03.420
You're crazy! That thing's
still in the design phase!

62
00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:07.430
[TOM laughs]

63
00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:06.640
[Tom laughs]

64
00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:09.380
[all laugh]

65
00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:11.770
<b>Kokoro
A Beautiful Secretary
Tom's Workers</b>

66
00:04:09.380 --> 00:04:12.050
You're still rowdy
after all this time, I see!

67
00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.990
You must be an orphan, huh?

68
00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.950
I can put in a good word
with our captain for you!

69
00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:26.160
You guys are pirates, right?

70
00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.750
[Oden]
What of it?

71
00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.170
Then no thanks, mister!

72
00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:31.540
A buncha pirates just
dumped me off here.

73
00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:33.170
Did they, now?

74
00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.550
[laughs]

75
00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:37.920
Never mind, then! [laughs]

76
00:04:57.570 --> 00:05:01.910
<b>Tequila Wolf
A Country on a Bridge</b>

77
00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:17.840
<b>Sabaody Archipelago</b>

78
00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:22.380
Off we go!

79
00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:32.810
[Oden]
This is Fishman Island!

80
00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.940
I've been here with White-kichi!

81
00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:36.940
Best not to drop
your guard, everyone!

82
00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:40.200
It's no less deadly
the second time around!

83
00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:46.130
Hey, Rayleigh! Did you hear
someone speak just now?

84
00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.470
You hearin' voices?

85
00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:49.560
There's no one
all the way down here.

86
00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.890
[Oden]
No, I heard it, too.

87
00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:53.930
[Gold Roger]
Glad I'm not alone, Oden!

88
00:05:53.930 --> 00:05:57.690
But who could be calling out
to us 10,000 leagues deep?

89
00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.620
[TOM laughs]

90
00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:01.660
[Oden]
See, Toki?
That's Fishman Island!

91
00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:02.450
[ODEN]
See, Toki?
That's Fishman Island!

92
00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:04.620
[Oden]
See, Toki?
That's Fishman Island!

93
00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:04.780
[TOKI]
How remarkable! [Toki]
How remarkable!

94
00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:05.790
[Toki]
How remarkable!

95
00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:09.620
An entire city encased
in a giant bubble!

96
00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:11.080
Oh, look!

97
00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:12.660
[Oden]
Fishmen soldiers?

98
00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:14.040
[Toki]
We're surrounded.

99
00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.960
[Neptune]
State your business,
surface dwellers!

100
00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:19.800
[Gold Roger]
Whoa there,
no need to blow the man down!

101
00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:23.590
Don't you recognize me,
Neptune? It's me, Roger!

102
00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.050
Roger? Ah, yes, I see now!

103
00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:30.640
So you're the foretold ones?

104
00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:37.630
<b>Mermaid Cove
Ryugu Kingdom</b>

105
00:06:30.900 --> 00:06:33.520
[Gold Roger]
I assure you, we're
not up to anything crooked.

106
00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:36.570
A man of your stature
scared of a little prophecy?

107
00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:38.240
You're better than that!

108
00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:40.160
It had cautioned us
that, very soon,

109
00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:43.120
someone will destroy
the gates of Fishman Island!

110
00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:47.000
Then suddenly you arrived,
so I'm a bit wary, you see!

111
00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.330
- [thud]
- [gasps]

112
00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.380
King Neptune,
it's been shattered!

113
00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:54.210
The Sea Kings are
chewing up the gate!

114
00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:57.550
Huh?! They're too gentle
to do such a thing.

115
00:06:57.550 --> 00:06:58.930
It can't be!

116
00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:00.840
[Oden]
It came true!

117
00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:03.640
[Fishman guard A]
There's a hole
in the outer bubble!

118
00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:06.730
[Neptune]
Go and seal it up this instant!

119
00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.440
So the prophecy was real!

120
00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:11.400
And you nearly
killed us over it!

121
00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:18.880
<b>Sharley
Prophet Girl
(Three Years Old)</b>

122
00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.190
The Sea Kings are
in a restless state.

123
00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:18.900
They are waiting for
the Mermaid Princess to be born.

124
00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:21.950
"Princess"? That means
there's another prophecy.

125
00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:24.280
So, the king should
expect a baby?

126
00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:26.040
How wonderful!

127
00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.370
Wait a moment!

128
00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:29.830
I can't have a child
before I've chosen a bride!

129
00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:31.080
And it's far too soon,

130
00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:33.420
I only took up the throne
a few months ago!

131
00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:35.960
I'd trust the prophet, my lord.

132
00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:38.590
She foresaw the death of
the former king exactly.

133
00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.590
Her track record is solid.

134
00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.850
And she was right
about that beautiful...

135
00:07:44.850 --> 00:07:48.350
uh, sorry. I mean that
dreadful mermaid Otohime

136
00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:48.820
and her political
protest as well!

137
00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:50.820
Otohime?

138
00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:54.030
Uh, certainly,
ill tidings, that one.

139
00:07:53.700 --> 00:08:01.460
<b>Deepwater Grove
Ryugu Kingdom</b>

140
00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:59.330
[Neptune]
Those prophecies
have been riling up

141
00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.080
our entire kingdom, as of late.

142
00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.340
[Gaban]
While that's interesting,

143
00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:04.340
we didn't come down here

144
00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:06.500
to catch up on
small talk, Neptune.

145
00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:08.670
Oh! I nearly forgot.

146
00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.760
How's the progress?

147
00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:13.180
Well. I presumed
two stones would

148
00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.560
provide us with
a clearer picture.

149
00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:17.350
But it seems to be
quite the opposite!

150
00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:17.810
It's an apology letter from
someone named Joyboy.

151
00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:20.220
This is an apology from
someone named Joyboy.

152
00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:20.430
[Neptune]
Incredible.

153
00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:21.020
[NEPTUNE]
Incredible.

154
00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:21.510
[Neptune]
Incredible.

155
00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:23.850
This man can really
transcribe them?

156
00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:23.900
[Gold Roger]
Oh, yes.

157
00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:24.560
[GOLD ROGER]
Oh, yes.

158
00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:25.310
[Gold Roger]
Oh yes.

159
00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:28.570
Have you heard of a weapon
that controls the Sea Kings?

160
00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:30.240
A weapon, you say?

161
00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:32.030
The stone on the sky island said

162
00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:34.030
this is where it
would be located.

163
00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:37.040
An Ancient Weapon with
the name of a god.

164
00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:40.330
"Poseidon," it's called.

165
00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:46.800
Well, truthfully, that does
line up with Sharley's prophecy.

166
00:08:46.800 --> 00:08:49.050
Though the implications of it
are rather chilling.

167
00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:50.970
Every few centuries,

168
00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:52.050
Every few centuries,
a mermaid who can

169
00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:53.260
a mermaid who can speak
to Sea Kings is born here,

170
00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.220
speak to Sea Kings is born here,

171
00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:58.060
and Sharley said
one is coming soon.

172
00:09:00.580 --> 00:09:00.850
I fear that she will
be my daughter. I fear that mermaid
will be my daughter.

173
00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:03.250
I fear that she will
be my daughter.

174
00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:03.450
Hard to believe
your soon-to-be little girl Hard to believe your
soon-to-be little girl

175
00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:05.300
Hard to believe
your soon-to-be little girl

176
00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:08.050
is a weapon that can
destroy the world.

177
00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:10.720
[Neptune]
I'm telling myself
it's just a prediction.

178
00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:13.560
And obviously,
a deadly weapon is only deadly

179
00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:15.040
if you use it as such.

180
00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:15.150
Who could have guessed that
Poseidon would be a Mermaid.

181
00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:18.940
Who could have guessed that
Poseidon would be a mermaid!

182
00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:25.100
So, Sharley, when will this
Mermaid Princess be born?

183
00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:29.610
So, Sharley. When will this
Mermaid Princess be born?

184
00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:36.730
This many!

185
00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:38.150
Seems we still have a decade.

186
00:09:38.150 --> 00:09:40.740
Seems we still have a decade.
Though, I must ask...

187
00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:43.070
why would you take an interest
in such a weapon?

188
00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:44.660
I'm disappointed in you!

189
00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:45.950
You're wrong, Neptune.

190
00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:47.200
We're not after the weapon.

191
00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:48.830
The people who left
the treasure behind

192
00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:50.370
were the ones
who called it that!

193
00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:52.500
I promise we're just
after their riches!

194
00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:55.250
[laughs]
Are you feeling better?

195
00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:56.540
Rest assured, old friend!

196
00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.420
We will not be coming
back in the future

197
00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:00.340
to kidnap your
hairy fish daughter!

198
00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.340
[gasps]
She won't be hairy!

199
00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:06.300
[Roger pirates laugh]

200
00:10:23.050 --> 00:10:25.600
We're nearing the Land of Wano!

201
00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.600
Ready to check out this stone?

202
00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:29.890
[Roger pirates]
Yeah!

203
00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.030
Huh?

204
00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:51.790
[panting]

205
00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:53.710
Oden, hey!

206
00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:54.090
<b>In 

the Seas

Near Wano</b>

207
00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:01.340
Something wrong, Redtaro?

208
00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.010
I think Lady Toki is sick!

209
00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.680
Where is she?

210
00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:11.860
[panting]

211
00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:14.150
[Oden]
Toki! Don't you worry!

212
00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:16.360
I am right here with you!

213
00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:21.030
Want my advice?

214
00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:22.160
[Oden]
Huh?

215
00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:23.780
Toki's traveled
the world with you,

216
00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:25.580
but there's something
that should be considered.

217
00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:28.460
Her original destination
was Wano.

218
00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:30.710
I'm a bit concerned
for her well being.

219
00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:33.040
She's been at sea
for a long time.

220
00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.580
Her fatigue is
catching up with her.

221
00:11:35.580 --> 00:11:39.210
I'll give it to ya straight.
If she presses on, she'll die.

222
00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.170
She ought to disembark at Wano.

223
00:11:41.170 --> 00:11:44.150
Don't risk it.
Toki is quite unwell.

224
00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:45.740
[CAT VIPER]
Kin'emon and
the others don't know

225
00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:47.660
about Toki or your children yet,

226
00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:50.490
so Dogstorm and I will be
happy to accompany her.

227
00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:52.540
They'll want a familiar
face or two around.

228
00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.830
It takes time to adjust
to a new home.

229
00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:58.330
We'll take good care of them.
I don't want you-gara to worry.

230
00:11:58.330 --> 00:12:00.800
I will stay, too... [gasps]

231
00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:03.460
Toki?

232
00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:10.260
I forbid it. You must go.

233
00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:11.740
Stop being foolish!

234
00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:12.820
You're not the type of man

235
00:12:12.820 --> 00:12:16.200
who would give up
halfway. Do it!

236
00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:18.210
[gasps]

237
00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:21.460
You must go on, or face divorce!

238
00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:34.530
these rags are not
ours by choice!

239
00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:37.030
We have eagerly been
waiting for your return,

240
00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:39.990
as we have unfortunate news!

241
00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:42.910
I know you left Kuri
in our hands,

242
00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:46.000
and we do apologize,
as we have tried our best!

243
00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:48.580
However, something wicked
has taken over Wano.

244
00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:50.040
[Toki]
One moment.

245
00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:51.540
You care for Oden, right?

246
00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.500
Then I must implore you to stop.

247
00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:57.050
Please, I beg of you,
let him go!

248
00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:04.170
[Oden]
I am leaving again,
at least for a time.

249
00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:15.110
[Oden]
Even as I turned my back
on the Land of Wano,

250
00:13:15.110 --> 00:13:18.410
I could tell something
about my home was amiss.

251
00:13:18.410 --> 00:13:21.000
If I had stayed
but a moment longer,

252
00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:24.120
I knew I would never
return to sea.

253
00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:28.540
[all]
– How could you do this, Lord Oden?
– How could you do this, Lord Oden?

254
00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:31.260
You damn jackass!

255
00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:35.130
[Oden]
I quickly took a copy
my country's Poneglyph

256
00:13:35.130 --> 00:13:38.930
and hurried back to Roger's ship
before I could learn more.

257
00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:42.350
It was my first time home
in four years,

258
00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:45.100
yet I only stayed mere hours.

259
00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:51.780
Jackass indeed!

260
00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:55.240
Then read the glyphs yourself
if you feel that way!

261
00:13:56.620 --> 00:13:59.530
Apologies, Oden. Thank you.

262
00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:08.100
[Oden]
We then headed to Cat
Viper and Dogstorm's homeland,

263
00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:10.310
the Mokomo Dukedom.

264
00:14:10.970 --> 00:14:14.170
A country that's carried
on the back of an elephant.

265
00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:15.710
Hope this works. [Hirugashi laughs]

266
00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:18.300
They say you can only find Zou
with the help of a Vivre card.

267
00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:21.680
[Zunesha trumpets]

268
00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:27.810
[gasps]
You're right! It's not
an island but a large pachyderm!

269
00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:31.350
[Gold Roger]
Oh.

270
00:14:31.350 --> 00:14:34.600
[Oden]
Huh? Who is speaking
to me? Who's voice is this?

271
00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:37.230
Hey, Oden. Is there
something bothering you?

272
00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:42.070
Sorry. It is nothing really.
Just a strange feeling.

273
00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:46.030
<b>Mokomo Dukedom</b>

274
00:14:48.830 --> 00:14:53.960
<b>Duke Genghis Baan</b>
<b>Mokomo Dukedom</b>

275
00:14:50.580 --> 00:14:54.170
We have received a letter
from Dogstorm and Cat Viper.

276
00:14:54.170 --> 00:14:56.290
They survived, did they?

277
00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.710
I assumed the worst!

278
00:14:58.710 --> 00:15:02.050
It was quite the fuss when those
naughty boys went missing.

279
00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:05.140
Thank you-gara for
relaying this message.

280
00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:13.980
There's an uneasy
feeling in the air.

281
00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:17.270
It's not like you to worry.
It must be something bad.

282
00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:18.980
I can sense it, too.

283
00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.940
You, too, Captain Roger?

284
00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.450
[Gold Roger]
It feels as if
there's some enormous presence

285
00:15:23.450 --> 00:15:25.910
and it's watching
our every move.

286
00:15:40.150 --> 00:15:40.250
[GOLD ROGER]
There it is!

287
00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.240
There it is!

288
00:15:41.240 --> 00:15:43.720
We found the last
Road Poneglyph!

289
00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:45.970
[Oden]
The Kozuki Clan crest!

290
00:15:45.970 --> 00:15:48.430
The Mink Tribe are
our brethren after all.

291
00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:50.310
Just as the stories say!

292
00:15:56.710 --> 00:15:57.080
I want to go!

293
00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:58.620
I beg you-gara!

294
00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:02.210
Hey, kiddo. You still have
some growing to do.

295
00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:03.340
[gasps]

296
00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:06.260
But don't worry,
you'll get your chance.

297
00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:08.300
Just gotta wait your turn, eh?

298
00:16:08.300 --> 00:16:10.600
[gasps]
And what does that mean?

299
00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:14.020
[Gold Roger]
When the time
comes, I want you to help me.

300
00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:19.400
[giggles]
Promise I will!
I'll be waiting for you-gara!

301
00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:22.020
[Gold Roger]
Take care of yourself, Pedro.

302
00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:26.900
[Oden]
Over the course of the journey,

303
00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:29.200
we acquired several
Real Poneglyphs

304
00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:31.660
and all four Road Poneglyphs.

305
00:16:31.660 --> 00:16:35.450
The end of our adventure
was drawing ever closer.

306
00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:40.650
<b>In a Port Town</b>

307
00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:45.260
Captain! Are you okay?

308
00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:56.480
Have you boys figured out
where we're headed yet?

309
00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:56.580
Yeah! Good to go!

310
00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:57.660
[all]
Yeah!

311
00:16:58.230 --> 00:17:00.480
How soon should we set out?

312
00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:02.650
Immediately, of course!

313
00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:06.360
Let's go!

314
00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:10.510
[Shanks]
Hey, Buggy? Buggy!

315
00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:15.300
[Oden]
Whether it was
good fortune or bad,

316
00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.300
the apprentice
Buggyjiro suddenly

317
00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.100
came down with a high fever.

318
00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:23.100
He had stay behind and forgo
the final step of the voyage.

319
00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:24.400
Don't have what it
takes to make it

320
00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:25.860
to the end of the trip, huh?

321
00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:27.230
What a shame.

322
00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:30.230
You shut up! I told you
I'm feeling better now!

323
00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:32.820
You're burning up so much
your face is red!

324
00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.490
Just relax and sleep.

325
00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:37.030
Say my nose is red again,
I dare you!

326
00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.450
I said your face!

327
00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:39.660
Attaboy!

328
00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:40.910
That's the spirit!

329
00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:44.830
Don't encourage
those two. Come on.

330
00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:48.420
All that treasure is
waiting for me, though!

331
00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:50.000
Stop pushing yourself!

332
00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:52.130
I refuse to stay here!

333
00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:53.180
[gasps]

334
00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:59.140
Please, sir! You gotta
take me with you!

335
00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:03.940
Just give it up already.
You need sleep.

336
00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:06.600
[Oden]
Despite them always
being at each other throats,

337
00:18:06.600 --> 00:18:10.070
Redtaro took it upon himself
to look after him.

338
00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:12.610
Honestly, it's hard
to tell if they're

339
00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:15.360
friends or enemies at times.

340
00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:20.910
Please let me go
with you. I'm fine.

341
00:18:22.940 --> 00:18:25.020
[Oden]
While we know
how Buggyjiro feels,

342
00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:26.610
what's your opinion on it?

343
00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:28.150
You're all right with staying?

344
00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:32.150
[Shanks]
Oden. Captain.
We'll make it out there one day,

345
00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:34.990
but when we do,
it should be on our own ship!

346
00:19:09.860 --> 00:19:11.360
[bell tolling]

347
00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:11.450
It says that the
Roger Pirates finally did it!

348
00:19:11.450 --> 00:19:13.820
[TOWNSPERSON A]
It says the
Roger Pirates finally did it!

349
00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:14.280
They just made history!

350
00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:15.620
[TOWNSPERSON B]
They just made history!

351
00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:17.000
That's the first time
a crew traveled

352
00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:18.700
all the way around the globe!

353
00:19:18.700 --> 00:19:19.040
He's conquered it all,
from beginning to end!

354
00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:20.330
[TOWNSPERSON C]
He's conquered it all,

355
00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:21.710
from beginning to end!

356
00:19:21.710 --> 00:19:22.080
Gold Roger! King of the sea!

357
00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:24.460
[TOWNSPERSON D]
Gold Roger...king of the sea!

358
00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:27.340
And the King of the Pirates!

359
00:19:27.340 --> 00:19:29.720
